------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Theorem B for two-tier L with image equality in the strict model 𝔉,
-- complete (the analogue of CaTTExp.Surface.ImageCatt).
--
-- The strict model. A cell over Γ is a tower of chains of K(Γ) (the
-- Gray unfolding of CaTTExp.Gray.Support), and the top chain of a
-- coherence coh_{Δ, t →_A u} in an environment ρ is
--
--   cohTL Δ A t u ρ = F_ρ (0 in the coherence case, the top chain of
--                          the total cell T(Δ) = ⟨Θ₁⟩ ⊗ … ⊗ ⟨Θₙ⟩
--                          otherwise)
--
-- with F_ρ = applyF (envTops ρ) the chain map sending a tuple
-- (w₁ … wₘ) to top(ρ w₁) ⊗ … ⊗ top(ρ wₘ). This is the formula of
-- Support.topS with the tops of ρ in place of those of a substitution
-- (a match of definitions only: no lemma here links cohTL to
-- Gray.Support.topS or to Strict.L.towerOf).
--
-- Identities (`UnitL`). An identity 1-cell is the empty tuple (the
-- unit of the hom complex): top chain [()], source ≈ target. A higher
-- identity has top chain 0 and source ≈ target.
--
-- Strict unitality on the four whisker heads (HR0L, HRL, HL0L, HLL):
--
--  * the coherence case never applies to a head (Gray.CohDim: it would
--    put the source above dim K(Γ)); for k = 0 this is
--    Gray.WhiskerZeroSide.nc0 / Gray.WhiskerZeroLeftSide.ncL;
--  * k ≥ 1: the head lives on Σ(BK k j) (or Σ(LK k j)), a single hom,
--    whose top chain is the sum of its top-dimensional cells as
--    1-tuples (`topΣ`); as a bag these are the top-dimensional
--    variables of BK k j (`GW`), computed in Surface.ImageCatt
--    (Wb-BK0, Wb-BK, Wb-LK). So the top chain is x + h for j = 0 and
--    x for j > 0, and an identity h of dimension ≥ 2 has top 0;
--  * k = 0: BK 0 j = W (Dsk j) and LK 0 j = LW (Dsk j)
--    (Gray.WhiskerZero, Gray.WhiskerZeroLeft), whose top chain is the
--    single tuple (x, h), resp. (h, x); an identity 1-cell h has top
--    [()], the unit of ⊗.
--
-- Result (`Instance`, from CaTTExp.Surface.WhiskerImage): TheoremB.Hyp
-- and Thm instantiated for two-tier L with every hypothesis
-- discharged, for the surface equality generated by image equality in
-- 𝔉 (CaTTExp.Surface.Generated). So `kc-from-el` holds for two-tier L
-- with this ≈ with no open module parameter. `conservative-from-el`
-- still takes the side-condition hypothesis (SC, `SideResp`) as an
-- argument; SC for this ≈ is not proved here (part of Lemma 1.3 of
-- the note).
------------------------------------------------------------------------
